                <pb facs="0279" n="1239" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1239"/>

                <head>No. 817.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Whitehouse.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 6,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 158.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch No. 175, of
                    the 29th ultimo, relative to the case of Shields and Wilson, whose extradition
                    has been demanded, and have transmitted a copy of the same to the
                    Attorney-General for his further information.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
